		"The live check did not run at implementation time: the copied auth.ason's token had expired, and the refresh got HTTP 400 invalid_grant. Refresh tokens rotate and can be used only once, so a copy shared with the old Hal breaks as soon as either side refreshes. The OAuth contract (headers, identity block, ?beta=true) is still unverified against the real API. Copy fresh credentials right before the first real request. Later (2026-09-26) the user refreshed the copy and real conversations with thinking and tool calls worked, so the OAuth contract is verified.",
